s, but this requires writing custom wrapper code for each use case and ensuring proper cleanup of temporary resources. This approach is error-prone and adds unnecessary complexity.\n\n## Proposed Behavior\nAnyIO should provide asynchronous context managers and utilities that mirror Python's tempfile module functionality. These should support async file operations, automatically clean up resources when exiting the context, and integrate seamlessly with AnyIO's existing async file I/O capabilities.\n\n## Additional Context\nThe implementation should handle all common tempfile use cases including anonymous temporary files, named temporary files, spooled temporary files (in-memory until a size threshold), and temporary directories. These should work with both binary and text modes.\n\nSee TASK_ENVIRONMENT.md for the actual public-version environment. Original preinstalled private tests are unavailable. Preserve existing tests; do not change them to conceal failures."}

